// §10 third-party schema survey — SpiceDB's own "group membership and
// parent-of/child-of relations" example. Source (fetched verbatim):
// https://raw.githubusercontent.com/authzed/examples/main/schemas/docs-style-sharing/schema-and-data.yaml
// README (fetched verbatim, same directory): "Access can be granted via
// direct access, or by being member of a group (that can be a child of
// another group) that has access to the resource." The fixture's own
// assertFalse proves real sibling-group isolation: an analyst (member of
// the `analysis` group only) cannot view a document shared only with the
// `engineering` group, even though both share a common parent (`company`).
//
// Disclosed restructuring, not a semantic gap: the source's
// `document.viewer` is typed `user | group_with_parent#view |
// group_with_child#view`, nesting into a *permission* on each group
// type. This compiler's `#` syntax can only name a genuine relation.
//   - `group_with_child#view` is a pure alias (`permission view = child`,
//     no other term) — swapping it for `group_with_child#child` (the
//     underlying relation) is exactly equivalent, not a simplification.
//   - `group_with_parent#view` is NOT a pure alias (`member | parent->
//     member`), so it can't be substituted the same way. Instead
//     `document.viewer` is split by target type: `viewer` keeps
//     `user | group_with_child#child`, and a new `viewer_group:
//     group_with_parent` relation carries the group_with_parent case,
//     reached via `viewer_group->view` (a tupleset traversal into that
//     group's real `view` permission — semantically identical to the
//     original's `group_with_parent#view` nesting).

namespace group_with_parent {
  relation parent: group_with_parent
  relation member: user

  permission view = member | parent->member
}

namespace group_with_child {
  relation child: user | group_with_child#child

  permission view = child
}

namespace document {
  relation viewer: user | group_with_child#child
  relation viewer_group: group_with_parent

  permission view = viewer | viewer_group->view
}
